response:
{
  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "Witnessing someone commit a violent assault that causes deep lacerations creates a moral—and in many places a legal—obligation to report. Reporting helps ensure the victim receives medical care and protection, allows authorities to investigate and prevent further harm, and fulfills a civic duty that typically outweighs personal loyalty. If you fear for your safety, you can report anonymously, contact victim services, or consult a lawyer; you can also encourage your friend to surrender and make sure the injured person gets immediate help. Exact legal duties vary by jurisdiction, so seek local legal or emergency guidance if unsure."
}

