  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "If the push was deliberate, aggressive, caused injury, or created a safety risk, it is appropriate to report it to on-site security or the police — the fact the responsible person is a parent does not exempt violent or dangerous behavior. If the incident was a minor accidental bump that was quickly resolved, reporting is usually unnecessary and de-escalation or letting the parties handle it is reasonable. Also consider the victim’s wishes: if they want to report, assist them; if you witness potential child endangerment or abuse by the parent, notify the appropriate authorities regardless of others’ preferences."
}

