response:
{
  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "Removing boxed merchandise through a side entrance and lifting a latch is suspicious and could be theft regardless of the relationship between the parties. You should not assume permission simply because the person is a son or daughter. The appropriate action is to verify authorization and follow company/store policy: notify a manager or loss-prevention/security so they can confirm whether the removal is permitted. Avoid confronting the person alone, document what you observed (time, location, description), and if management determines it is unauthorized, involve law enforcement. If you confirm the removal is authorized, no report is needed."
}

